WEBVTT

00:01.549 --> 00:02.675
KATARA: Water...

00:03.468 --> 00:04.761
Earth...

00:05.512 --> 00:06.971
Fire...

00:07.805 --> 00:09.140
Air.

00:09.724 --> 00:13.019
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:14.145 --> 00:17.941
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:18.483 --> 00:21.945
Only the Avatar, master of
all four elements, could stop them.

00:22.070 --> 00:25.698
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

00:25.823 --> 00:29.494
A hundred years passed and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar...

00:29.619 --> 00:31.412
An airbender named Aang.

00:32.080 --> 00:33.748
And although his airbending
skills are great,

00:33.873 --> 00:36.709
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:36.834 --> 00:37.961
AANG: Oof!

00:38.044 --> 00:41.089
But I believe Aang
can save the world.

00:41.548 --> 00:43.299
( ♪... )

00:46.928 --> 00:49.013
( MAN READING )

00:49.847 --> 00:52.350
You have no idea what this war
has put me through.

00:52.600 --> 00:53.893
Me personally.

00:54.310 --> 00:57.146
The Fire Nation took my mother
away from me.

00:58.189 --> 00:59.357
I'm sorry.

01:00.066 --> 01:03.570
You might have everyone else
here buying your transformation.

01:04.320 --> 01:06.197
But you and I both know
you've struggled with doing

01:06.281 --> 01:07.740
the right thing in the past.

01:07.991 --> 01:10.285
So let me tell you something
right now.

01:10.910 --> 01:14.455
You make one step backward, one slip-up,
give me one reason to think

01:14.539 --> 01:15.915
you might hurt Aang

01:16.541 --> 01:19.377
And you won't have to worry
about your destiny anymore.

01:24.757 --> 01:27.385
( BIRDS CHIRPING )

01:30.013 --> 01:33.016
( SNORING )

01:37.395 --> 01:38.771
( YAWNS )

01:40.648 --> 01:42.317
( APPA GRUNTS )

01:45.570 --> 01:47.447
( APPA GROWLS )

02:09.052 --> 02:10.053
ZUKO: Watch out!

02:10.261 --> 02:11.721
( GRUNTING )

02:11.846 --> 02:13.222
What are you doing?

02:13.306 --> 02:14.724
Keeping rocks from crushing you.

02:15.183 --> 02:18.061
Okay, I'm not crushed,
you can get off me now.

02:18.603 --> 02:20.647
I'll take that as a thank you.

02:23.274 --> 02:25.109
Come on, we can get out
through here.

02:25.360 --> 02:26.527
( MOMO CHATTERING )

02:26.819 --> 02:28.446
( GROANS ) What are you doing?

02:28.988 --> 02:31.115
Go ahead, I'll hold them off.

02:31.616 --> 02:33.409
I think this is a family visit.

02:33.534 --> 02:35.203
Zuko, no!

02:35.328 --> 02:37.497
Come on, we've got to
get out of here.

02:52.470 --> 02:53.930
What are you doing here?

02:54.180 --> 02:56.391
You mean it's not obvious yet?

02:56.516 --> 02:59.310
I am about to celebrate
becoming an only child.

03:04.440 --> 03:06.401
( SHOUTS )

03:32.969 --> 03:34.303
( APPA GROANS )

03:34.512 --> 03:35.930
AANG: I can't get him
to go in there.

03:36.055 --> 03:37.557
Appa hates tunnels.

03:37.890 --> 03:40.560
Aang, there's no way
we can fly out of here.

03:40.977 --> 03:42.645
AANG: We'll have to find a way.

03:43.104 --> 03:44.647
We need to split up.

03:44.772 --> 03:46.983
Take the tunnel and
get to the stolen airship.

03:48.317 --> 03:49.444
No.

03:49.819 --> 03:52.363
The Fire Nation can't
separate our family again.

03:52.613 --> 03:53.990
It'll be okay.

03:54.073 --> 03:55.074
It's not forever.

04:11.257 --> 04:13.843
I can clear that away and
we can fly out through there.

04:13.926 --> 04:17.513
Um, there's an awful lot of fire
in that general direction.

04:17.889 --> 04:18.973
We'll get through.

04:19.098 --> 04:20.099
Let's go.

04:22.602 --> 04:24.061
( APPA GROWLING )

04:34.864 --> 04:36.741
( MOMO CHATTERING )

04:56.636 --> 04:57.845
( APPA GROANS )

04:58.304 --> 04:59.305
( GRUNTS )

04:59.388 --> 05:02.558
( APPA GROANING )

05:21.869 --> 05:23.412
( GRUNTING )

05:24.956 --> 05:27.625
( GRUNTING )

05:30.002 --> 05:31.921
( APPA GROANS )

05:36.008 --> 05:37.802
She's not gonna make it.

05:43.891 --> 05:45.643
Of course, she did.

05:47.311 --> 05:49.689
( APPA GROANS )

05:54.110 --> 05:57.280
AANG: Wow, camping... It really seems like
old times again, doesn't it?

05:57.905 --> 06:01.117
If you really want it to feel
like old times, I could, uh...

06:01.242 --> 06:03.327
Chase you around awhile
and try to capture you.

06:03.452 --> 06:04.495
( LAUGHTER )

06:04.620 --> 06:06.163
Ha-ha.

06:07.123 --> 06:09.625
( SIGHS ) To Zuko.

06:09.750 --> 06:11.794
Who knew after all those times
he tried to snuff us out

06:11.919 --> 06:13.796
today he'd be our hero.

06:14.213 --> 06:15.673
ALL: Hear, hear.

06:16.799 --> 06:17.800
I'm touched.

06:18.092 --> 06:19.260
I don't deserve this.

06:19.677 --> 06:21.429
Yeah, no kidding.

06:23.139 --> 06:24.557
What's with her?

06:24.682 --> 06:26.142
I wish I knew.

06:28.269 --> 06:29.979
SOKKA: What's with him?

06:36.277 --> 06:37.778
This isn't fair.

06:38.029 --> 06:39.697
Everyone else
seems to trust me now.

06:39.864 --> 06:41.032
What is it with you?

06:41.115 --> 06:43.159
Oh, everyone trusts you now?

06:43.284 --> 06:45.578
I was the first person
to trust you, remember?

06:45.828 --> 06:47.288
Back in Ba Sing Se.

06:47.413 --> 06:50.499
And you turned around and
betrayed me, betrayed all of us.

06:51.667 --> 06:53.336
What can I do
to make it up to you?

06:53.878 --> 06:55.129
You really want to know?

06:55.463 --> 06:59.216
Hmm, maybe you could reconquer Ba Sing Se
in the name of the Earth King.

06:59.300 --> 07:02.053
Or, I know, you could
bring my mother back.

07:10.436 --> 07:11.562
Oops.

07:12.063 --> 07:13.230
Wrong tent.

07:13.481 --> 07:15.858
Sorry, do you need to
talk to Sokka too?

07:16.233 --> 07:17.860
Nope, not me.

07:21.906 --> 07:24.533
Well, hello.

07:24.867 --> 07:28.704
Uh, Zuko, yes, why would I be
expecting anyone different?

07:28.829 --> 07:31.207
( GULPS, COUGHS )

07:31.374 --> 07:32.458
So what's on your mind?

07:32.875 --> 07:36.253
Your sister, she hates me,
and I don't know why.

07:36.462 --> 07:38.172
But I do care
what she thinks of me.

07:38.547 --> 07:40.341
Nah, she doesn't hate you.

07:40.466 --> 07:42.093
Katara doesn't hate anyone.

07:42.426 --> 07:44.345
Except maybe some people
in the Fire Nation.

07:44.887 --> 07:48.057
No, I mean, uh, not people
who are good but used to be bad.

07:48.182 --> 07:49.892
I mean bad people.

07:50.142 --> 07:51.644
Fire Nation people who are still bad,

07:51.811 --> 07:53.604
who've never been good
and probably won't be ever.

07:53.688 --> 07:54.689
Stop.

07:55.106 --> 07:56.524
Okay, listen...

07:57.233 --> 07:59.110
I know this may seem
out of nowhere

07:59.610 --> 08:01.696
but I want you to tell me
what happened to your mother.

08:01.988 --> 08:02.989
What?

08:03.197 --> 08:04.407
Why would you want to know that?

08:04.490 --> 08:07.660
Katara mentioned it before when we were
in prison together in Ba Sing Se

08:08.202 --> 08:10.329
and again just now
when she was yelling at me.

08:10.955 --> 08:12.748
I think somehow...

08:13.082 --> 08:16.252
She's connected her anger
about that to her anger at me.

08:17.628 --> 08:19.380
It's not a day I like to remember.

08:26.345 --> 08:28.305
( LAUGHING )

08:34.186 --> 08:36.230
I'm going to find mom.

08:39.025 --> 08:41.485
SOKKA: Many of the warriors had
seen the black snow before

08:41.610 --> 08:43.529
and they knew what it meant...

08:43.654 --> 08:45.448
A Fire Nation raid.

08:45.573 --> 08:47.366
( SCREAMING )

08:51.120 --> 08:52.913
( SCREAMING )

08:56.250 --> 08:59.962
SOKKA: We were badly outnumbered,
but somehow we managed to drive them off.

09:04.341 --> 09:07.094
As quickly as they came,
they just left.

09:10.598 --> 09:12.933
I was so relieved
when it was over

09:13.059 --> 09:15.311
but that's because I didn't
know yet what had happened.

09:16.228 --> 09:18.105
I didn't know
we'd lost our mother.

09:18.481 --> 09:22.443
Wait, can you remember any details about
the soldiers who raided your village?

09:22.860 --> 09:25.029
Like what the lead ship
looked like?

09:25.488 --> 09:27.907
Yeah... Sea ravens.

09:28.074 --> 09:30.493
The main ship had flags
with sea ravens on them.

09:31.035 --> 09:32.828
The symbol of
the southern raiders.

09:33.662 --> 09:34.747
Thanks, Sokka.

09:34.872 --> 09:36.123
No problem.

09:36.248 --> 09:38.459
Thanks for stopping by.

09:38.876 --> 09:40.753
( SIGHS ) Thought
he'd never leave.

09:42.880 --> 09:44.215
Suki?

09:45.883 --> 09:47.718
( WHISTLING )

09:56.352 --> 09:57.728
You look terrible.

09:58.354 --> 09:59.730
I waited out here all night.

09:59.939 --> 10:01.190
What do you want?

10:01.524 --> 10:03.234
I know who killed your mother.

10:03.317 --> 10:04.693
I'm going to help you find him.

10:14.829 --> 10:16.372
I need to borrow Appa.

10:16.956 --> 10:19.834
Why, is it your turn to take
a little field trip with Zuko?

10:20.084 --> 10:21.752
Yes, it is.

10:22.837 --> 10:25.256
Oh... What's going on?

10:25.464 --> 10:28.008
We're going to find the man
who took my mother from me.

10:28.676 --> 10:30.427
ZUKO: Sokka told me
the story of what happened.

10:30.636 --> 10:33.430
I know who did it,
and I know how to find him.

10:33.681 --> 10:36.851
Um, and what exactly do you
think this will accomplish?

10:37.810 --> 10:40.187
( SCOFFS ) I knew
you wouldn't understand.

10:40.729 --> 10:43.274
Wait, stop, I do understand.

10:43.607 --> 10:45.776
You're feeling unbelievable
pain and rage.

10:46.360 --> 10:49.446
How do you think I felt about
the sandbenders when they stole Appa?

10:50.156 --> 10:51.949
How do you think I felt
about the Fire Nation

10:52.032 --> 10:53.826
when I found out what happened
to my people?

10:54.160 --> 10:55.536
ZUKO: She needs this, Aang.

10:55.661 --> 10:58.247
This is about getting closure
and justice.

10:58.372 --> 10:59.623
I don't think so.

10:59.748 --> 11:01.500
I think it's about
getting revenge.

11:01.625 --> 11:02.835
KATARA: Fine, maybe it is.

11:02.960 --> 11:04.753
Maybe that's what I need.

11:04.879 --> 11:06.755
Maybe that's what he deserves.

11:06.881 --> 11:09.133
Katara, you sound like Jet.

11:09.258 --> 11:10.467
It's not the same.

11:10.676 --> 11:11.969
Jet attacked the innocent.

11:12.178 --> 11:14.180
This man, he's a monster.

11:14.430 --> 11:16.223
Katara, she was my mother too.

11:16.473 --> 11:18.559
But I think Aang might be right.

11:19.059 --> 11:20.895
Then you didn't love her
the way I did.

11:21.187 --> 11:22.479
Katara...

11:23.814 --> 11:27.318
The monks used to say that revenge
is like a two-headed rat viper.

11:27.902 --> 11:30.905
While you watch your enemy go down,
you're being poisoned yourself.

11:31.572 --> 11:34.283
That's cute, but this isn't
air temple preschool.

11:34.700 --> 11:36.118
It's the real world.

11:36.243 --> 11:38.162
Now that I know
he's out there...

11:38.287 --> 11:40.122
Now that I know
we can find him...

11:40.247 --> 11:41.874
I feel like I have no choice.

11:42.416 --> 11:44.668
Katara, you do have a choice.

11:44.960 --> 11:46.212
Forgiveness.

11:46.462 --> 11:48.214
That's the same as
doing nothing.

11:48.547 --> 11:50.132
No, it's not.

11:50.424 --> 11:53.802
It's easy to do nothing,
but it's hard to forgive.

11:53.928 --> 11:57.181
It's not just hard,
it's impossible.

12:07.775 --> 12:09.985
So you were just gonna
take Appa anyway?

12:10.945 --> 12:11.946
Yes.

12:12.154 --> 12:14.448
It's okay, because I forgive you.

12:15.866 --> 12:17.451
That give you any ideas?

12:17.618 --> 12:19.119
Don't try to stop us.

12:19.495 --> 12:21.205
I wasn't planning to.

12:21.330 --> 12:23.123
This is a journey
you need to take.

12:23.249 --> 12:25.042
You need to face this man.

12:27.253 --> 12:30.297
But when you do,
please don't choose revenge.

12:30.547 --> 12:33.467
Let your anger out,
and then let it go.

12:34.009 --> 12:35.135
Forgive him.

12:35.302 --> 12:38.514
Okay, we'll be sure to do that,
guru goody-goody.

12:38.764 --> 12:40.266
Thanks for understanding, Aang.

12:40.474 --> 12:41.517
Yip-yip.

12:42.184 --> 12:43.519
( APPA GROANING )

12:43.894 --> 12:45.646
You know, you're pretty wise
for a kid.

12:46.355 --> 12:47.481
Thanks, Sokka.

12:47.564 --> 12:49.858
Usually it's annoying, but
right now I'm just impressed.

12:50.192 --> 12:51.568
I appreciate that.

12:51.860 --> 12:53.779
So can I borrow Momo for a week?

12:54.071 --> 12:55.155
Why do you need Momo?

12:55.281 --> 12:56.448
( HUMS ) I don't know.

12:59.660 --> 13:02.371
ZUKO: We need to find the
fire navy communication tower.

13:02.663 --> 13:05.582
All the navy's movements are
coordinated by messenger hawk.

13:05.958 --> 13:08.669
And every tower has to be up to date
on where everyone is deployed.

13:09.295 --> 13:11.171
KATARA: So once we find
the communication tower

13:11.255 --> 13:13.382
we bust in and take
the information we need.

13:13.841 --> 13:15.134
ZUKO: Not exactly.

13:15.217 --> 13:17.720
We need to be stealthy
and make sure no one spots us.

13:18.137 --> 13:21.890
Otherwise, they'll warn the southern
raiders long before we reach them.

13:31.400 --> 13:33.402
( DOOR CREAKS )

13:47.708 --> 13:50.169
Okay, southern raiders.

13:52.338 --> 13:55.341
Bam, on patrol
near Whaletail Island.

13:56.175 --> 13:57.968
Whaletail Island,
here we come.

13:59.511 --> 14:01.847
( APPA GROANS )

14:06.977 --> 14:08.187
You should get some rest.

14:08.520 --> 14:09.813
We'll be there in a few hours.

14:10.314 --> 14:11.607
You'll need all your strength.

14:12.066 --> 14:13.776
Oh, don't you worry
about my strength.

14:13.901 --> 14:15.027
I have plenty.

14:15.361 --> 14:17.905
I'm not the helpless little girl
I was when they came.

14:22.034 --> 14:24.745
I'm going to find mom.

14:27.706 --> 14:29.500
Mom!

14:31.585 --> 14:33.128
MOTHER: Just let her go...

14:33.212 --> 14:35.089
and I'll give you
the information you want.

14:35.422 --> 14:37.758
You heard your mother...
Get out of here!

14:38.133 --> 14:40.010
Mom, I'm scared.

14:40.219 --> 14:41.387
Go find your dad, sweetie.

14:41.512 --> 14:42.513
I'll handle this.

14:50.437 --> 14:52.314
KATARA: I ran
as fast as I could.

14:52.481 --> 14:54.108
Dad, dad!

14:54.191 --> 14:55.984
Please, I think mom's
in trouble!

14:56.276 --> 14:57.444
There's a man in our house.

14:57.778 --> 14:58.821
Kya!

15:02.741 --> 15:04.410
KATARA: But we were too late.

15:05.119 --> 15:07.079
When we got there,
the man was gone...

15:07.663 --> 15:09.039
And so was she.

15:09.540 --> 15:11.166
Your mother was a brave woman.

15:13.794 --> 15:14.878
I know.

15:20.384 --> 15:22.636
There, see those
sea raven flags?

15:26.515 --> 15:28.142
ZUKO: It's the southern raiders.

15:28.350 --> 15:29.893
Let's do this.

15:37.860 --> 15:39.862
So there I was, and I was like,
you know, it was...

15:39.987 --> 15:41.447
( SCREAMS )

15:53.125 --> 15:54.376
( SCREAMING )

15:57.379 --> 15:59.214
( APPA SNORTS )

16:01.175 --> 16:02.759
( SCREAMS )

16:06.430 --> 16:07.431
( MAN GRUNTS )

16:12.311 --> 16:13.979
This is it, Katara.

16:14.062 --> 16:15.564
Are you ready to face him?

16:18.442 --> 16:19.443
( ROARS )

16:32.039 --> 16:33.248
Who are you?

16:33.332 --> 16:34.541
You don't remember her?

16:34.625 --> 16:36.376
You will soon, trust me.

16:40.088 --> 16:41.298
What's...

16:41.381 --> 16:43.342
( GRUNTING )

16:44.218 --> 16:45.552
Happening to me?

16:47.179 --> 16:48.347
( GROANS )

16:51.975 --> 16:53.101
Think back.

16:53.268 --> 16:56.063
Think back to your last raid
on the southern water tribe.

16:56.772 --> 16:58.607
I don't know what
you're talking about.

16:58.690 --> 17:00.067
Please, I don't know.

17:00.776 --> 17:02.027
Don't lie!

17:02.236 --> 17:05.072
You look her in the eye and you tell me
you don't remember what you did.

17:15.123 --> 17:16.208
It's not him.

17:17.876 --> 17:19.086
( GRUNTS )

17:19.670 --> 17:20.879
He's not the man.

17:21.004 --> 17:22.005
What?

17:22.089 --> 17:23.215
What do you mean he's not?

17:23.382 --> 17:24.883
He's the leader of
the southern raiders.

17:24.967 --> 17:26.301
He has to be the guy.

17:31.014 --> 17:32.266
( GRUNTING )

17:32.349 --> 17:34.643
If you're not the man
we're looking for, who is?

17:35.310 --> 17:37.062
You must be looking for Yon Rha.

17:37.396 --> 17:39.231
He retired four years ago.

17:51.368 --> 17:55.205
Yon Rha, you lazy piece of work,
I need something.

17:55.664 --> 17:56.999
Yes, mother.

17:57.499 --> 17:58.709
What is it?

17:58.875 --> 18:02.170
The tomato-carrot from your
garden are too hard for my gums.

18:02.379 --> 18:04.214
I need something soft and juicy.

18:04.923 --> 18:07.551
Would you like something else
from the garden?

18:07.759 --> 18:09.052
I would be happy to...

18:09.177 --> 18:10.512
Forget your stupid garden!

18:11.013 --> 18:14.391
Get your grimy heinie to the market
and buy me some real food.

18:17.811 --> 18:21.398
( THUNDER RUMBLING FAINTLY )

18:21.648 --> 18:24.526
( WIND CHIMES RINGING )

18:30.907 --> 18:32.159
Hello?

18:32.534 --> 18:34.119
Did you see someone?

18:44.463 --> 18:45.464
Hello?

18:45.672 --> 18:46.840
Is someone there?

18:50.052 --> 18:51.303
That was him.

18:51.428 --> 18:53.305
That was the monster.

18:58.602 --> 19:01.480
( THUNDER RUMBLING )

19:05.901 --> 19:07.986
Nobody sneaks up on me
without getting burned.

19:19.414 --> 19:20.791
( GRUNTS )

19:25.796 --> 19:27.673
We weren't behind the bush.

19:28.715 --> 19:31.009
And I wouldn't try
firebending again.

19:31.760 --> 19:34.888
Whoever you are, take my money,
take whatever you want.

19:35.097 --> 19:36.598
I'll cooperate.

19:38.016 --> 19:39.685
Do you know who I am?

19:40.310 --> 19:42.521
No... I'm not sure.

19:42.896 --> 19:45.607
Oh, you better remember me
like your life depends on it.

19:45.899 --> 19:47.776
Why don't you take
a closer look?

19:48.318 --> 19:52.280
Yes, yes, I remember you now.

19:53.073 --> 19:54.991
You're the little
water tribe girl.

19:55.367 --> 19:57.035
( THUNDER CRASHES )

19:57.119 --> 19:59.621
Just let her go and I'll give
you the information you want.

19:59.955 --> 20:01.164
You heard your mother.

20:01.456 --> 20:03.041
Get out of here.

20:03.125 --> 20:05.001
Mom, I'm scared.

20:05.168 --> 20:06.586
Go find your dad, sweetie.

20:06.753 --> 20:08.088
I'll handle this.

20:11.466 --> 20:14.594
Now tell me...
Who is it?

20:15.011 --> 20:16.888
Who's the waterbender?

20:17.139 --> 20:19.683
There are no waterbenders here.

20:19.891 --> 20:22.769
The Fire Nation took them
all away a long time ago.

20:22.894 --> 20:23.937
You're lying.

20:24.187 --> 20:29.151
My source says there's one waterbender
left in the southern water tribe.

20:29.276 --> 20:32.612
We're not leaving
until we find the waterbender.

20:32.821 --> 20:36.241
If I tell you, do you promise to leave
the rest of the village alone?

20:37.242 --> 20:38.702
Mm.

20:39.828 --> 20:42.289
It's me... Take me
as your prisoner.

20:42.706 --> 20:45.751
I'm afraid I'm not
taking prisoners today.

20:48.336 --> 20:49.337
( GULPS )

20:50.005 --> 20:51.006
( THUNDER CRASHES )

20:51.089 --> 20:52.132
She lied to you.

20:52.215 --> 20:54.217
She was protecting
the last waterbender.

20:54.301 --> 20:55.302
What?

20:55.469 --> 20:56.511
Who?

20:57.721 --> 20:58.722
Me!

21:12.194 --> 21:13.361
( GRUNTS )

21:14.196 --> 21:15.322
( WHIMPERS )

21:28.835 --> 21:32.672
I did a bad thing, I know I did,
and you deserve revenge.

21:32.798 --> 21:34.508
So why don't you take my mother?

21:34.591 --> 21:35.759
That would be fair.

21:36.343 --> 21:39.304
I always wondered what kind of
person could do such a thing.

21:39.763 --> 21:42.641
But now that I see you,
I think I understand.

21:43.141 --> 21:46.770
There's just nothing inside you,
nothing at all.

21:47.062 --> 21:49.272
You're pathetic and sad
and empty.

21:49.356 --> 21:51.983
Please spare me. ( WHIMPERS )

21:52.359 --> 21:54.486
But as much as I hate you...

21:56.196 --> 21:57.864
I just can't do it.

22:04.454 --> 22:07.040
( YON RHA WHIMPERING )

22:17.467 --> 22:18.677
( APPA GROANS )

22:25.350 --> 22:27.143
Katara, are you okay?

22:28.228 --> 22:29.563
I'm doing fine.

22:30.939 --> 22:32.607
Zuko told me what you did.

22:32.983 --> 22:34.776
Or what you didn't do, I guess.

22:35.318 --> 22:36.403
I'm proud of you.

22:37.320 --> 22:38.530
I wanted to do it.

22:38.780 --> 22:42.033
I wanted to take out all my
anger at him, but I couldn't.

22:42.868 --> 22:45.579
I don't know if it's
because I'm too weak to do it

22:45.662 --> 22:48.039
or if it's because
I'm strong enough not to.

22:48.373 --> 22:49.666
AANG: You did the right thing.

22:49.875 --> 22:53.044
Forgiveness is the first step you have
to take to begin healing.

22:55.380 --> 22:58.758
But I didn't forgive him...
I'll never forgive him.

23:01.011 --> 23:03.179
But I am ready to forgive you.

23:10.020 --> 23:12.063
ZUKO: You were right
about what Katara needed.

23:12.689 --> 23:14.274
Violence wasn't the answer.

23:14.816 --> 23:16.151
It never is.

23:16.651 --> 23:18.653
Then I have a question for you.

23:19.738 --> 23:21.656
What are you gonna do
when you face my father?

23:33.251 --> 23:36.004
( MEN VOCALIZING RHYTHMICALLY )
